package prompt

const DiagramPrompt = `You design DEVS model structures. Return only JSON matching the schema.
Each model has a unique id, type atomic or coupled, ports with unique name and direction, and components containing the ids of its immediate child models. Atomic models have no components. Coupled models can contain other coupled models to any required depth. Include an enclosing coupled model unless the user explicitly requests independent models or a single atomic model.
Each connection MUST include owner: the id of the coupled model owning that connection. Its endpoints must be that owner or its immediate children. Internal couplings connect a child output to another child input; external input couplings connect an owner's input to a child's input; external output couplings connect a child's output to an owner's output. Route signals across levels through explicit coupled ports; never connect distant descendants directly. Containment cycles are forbidden, but feedback couplings between children (including self-feedback) are valid DEVS structures. Preserve logical model ids when refining an existing structure. Treat the supplied current structure as authoritative, including manual edits. Do not remove unrelated models. Return the complete updated structure, never a partial patch. Identifiers must not contain slashes or colons.`
